    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40226" root="نفر" body-key="n">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نِفْرٌ</span></b>  an imitative sequent to <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عِفْرٌ</span>, (T, M, K,)
and so is ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَفِرٌ</span></b>  to <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَفِرٌ</span>, (Sgh, K, but omitted in
some copies of the K,) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نِفْرِيَةٌ</span></b>  to <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عِفْرِيَةٌ</span>,
(T, M, K,) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نِفْرِيتٌ</span></b>  to <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عِفْرِيتٌ</span>, (T, S, M,
K,) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نُفَارِيَةٌ</span></b>  to <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُفَارِيَهٌ</span>, (T, M, K,) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نِفْرِيتَةٌ</span></b> 
to <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عِفرِيتَةٌ</span>; (K;) denoting corroboration. (S.)

